### Rules for Frontend

- You must pay attention to visual clarity and contrast. Do not place white text on a white background.
- You must ensure the UX is pleasant. Boxes should grow to fit their contents, etc. 
- When asking the user for sensitive information - you must use password style text-entry boxes in the UI.
- You should use Next.js as it works best with Vercel. 
- This frontend will ultimately be deployed on Vercel, but it should be possible to test locally. 
- Always provide users with a way to run the created UI once you have created it.

### Visual Identity
- Style: Clean academic meets modern SaaS. Think Notion meets Linear.
- Vibe: Focused, calm, and trustworthy — not flashy or gamified.

### Color Palette
- Background: #0F1117 (deep dark, near-black)
- Surface/Cards: #1C1E26
- Border: #2E3044
- Primary Accent: #7C6AF7 (soft violet — wisdom, intellect)
- Secondary Accent: #4ECDC4 (teal — for hints and nudges)
- Danger/Escape hatch: #FF6B6B (for "just tell me" button)
- Text Primary: #F0F0F5
- Text Muted: #8B8FA8

### Typography
- Font: Inter for UI, JetBrains Mono for code blocks
- Headings: Semi-bold, generous letter-spacing
- Body: 16px base, 1.6 line-height for readability

### Component Rules
- Rounded corners: 12px for cards, 8px for buttons/inputs
- Shadows: Subtle, dark-mode-friendly (no harsh drop shadows)
- Chat bubbles: User on the right (accent-colored), tutor on the left (surface-colored)
- Always render markdown and code blocks with syntax highlighting
- Streaming responses should show a subtle animated cursor while loading
- Never use default shadcn/Tailwind gray — always use the palette above
- Prefer framer-motion for transitions and chat bubble animations
- Streaming must be handled with the Fetch API using ReadableStream, not polling

### Layout
- Max content width: 800px centered (keeps reading comfortable)
- Sidebar for topic/difficulty selector, main area for chat
- Mobile responsive — stack sidebar above chat on small screens

### UI Copy & Tone
- Button labels should feel encouraging: "Give me a hint 💡" not "Hint"
- Escape hatch button: "I give up — just tell me 🏳️"
- Empty state: "What would you like to explore today?"
- Avoid robotic placeholder text like "Enter message here"